The city fire chief is appointed as emergency management director, and is charged with the following duties:
(1) Representing the governing officials of the city on matters pertaining to emergency management;
(2) Assisting the city officials in organizing city departments for emergency operations;
(3) Developing, in conjunction with city departments and agencies, the city plan for emergency functions set forth herein. Such plan will be in consonance with the state natural disaster operations plan and nuclear emergency operations plan, and shall be submitted to the mayor and the city council for their approval, and thence to the state emergency management agency for approval;
(4) Maintaining the emergency management office and carrying out the day-to-day administration of the city emergency management program, including the submission of required reports to the state emergency management agency;
(5) Submitting reports as required by the city council in keeping with good management practices; e.g., financial, daily activity, etc.;
(6) Procuring, with the approval of the city council, a facility to be used as the city emergency operations center;
(7) Coordinating the activities of the city emergency operations center staff during periods of a declared emergency under the supervision of the city council.
(Code 1990, § 7-2; Ord. No. 173, § II, 8-9-1983)
State Law reference— Local director required for state financial assistance, O.C.G.A. § 38-3-27(e)(1)(B).

